WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.850
I see, this is quite the bounded field.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.810
It looks impossible
to brute force yourself past it.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:10.150
I'd expect nothing less
from something the Edelfelts own.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.740
I'm honored to receive such compliments.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:17.910
I mean, not even the El-Melloi Princess
can find a way to escape from it.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:24.370
From ancient times,

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:30.420
various myths and legends have stated
that wealth springs from underground.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.680
Graves and the underworld have another
aspect of being storehouses for treasure.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.430
Sir!

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.890
In other words, you should hide
your treasured collection under the floor!

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.640
Like games, and those promissory notes
in safes hidden in underground labyrinths!

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.440
And secrets adults hold?

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:50.860
But sir, you have no need for such
because you have me.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:55.450
I'm always okay with personal lectures,
or rather I want to be your mistress!

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:01.200
All right, you guys, shut up right now
or get triple the homework. Take your pick.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.880
Kings stockpiled
immense fortunes in their graves

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:10.340
to continue their reign in the afterlife.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.170
For instance, the pharaohs of Egypt...

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.800
Babylonia's King of Heroes...

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:19.800
Gilgamesh...

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.060
Sorry, I'll continue with the lecture.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.320
From ancient times, it has been said
wealth springs from underground.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:34.440
Hold on, you've already covered that part.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:38.070
Oh, is that so? Sorry. Let's see...

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:41.490
<i>I don't know what he saw
during the Holy Grail War.</i>

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.870
<i>However, at the rate he's going,
he will become roped into more trouble.</i>

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.040
The Holy Grail War...

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:24.930
So...

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.600
what'd you want to talk about?

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.600
Um, well...

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.730
You're drawing this out.
There's something you want to ask, right?

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:36.360
And it's about your mentor,

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.610
my dear elder brother.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.530
It's about the Holy Grail War.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.950
Sir supposedly was a part
of this Holy Grail War in the past.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.330
What happened to him there?

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.790
That's what I want to know.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.290
So I see.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.220
Now, I don't mind talking to you about it,

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.970
but it's rather dull if I told you for free.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.300
Gaining information requires
a suitable compensation.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.720
Since you're here,

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:12.140
why don't you accompany me
in my hobbies?

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.060
Understood.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.360
This does look good on you
just as I thought!

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.530
Th-That's not true!
You can see my face, too!

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:32.200
It's fine. We're the only ones
in the dressing room.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.460
You promised me, right?

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.460
With over 150 years of tradition,

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.550
Carnac is one of London's
biggest department stores.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.970
As compensation, you agreed
to come with me on my shopping trip.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.720
But it's all been about me!

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.350
It's okay! It's okay!

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.730
You'll need winter clothes soon, right?

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.650
I will personally choose clothing for you.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.530
Isn't this a bit too daring?

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:08.200
Oh no, a Mage has to experience
all things. Experience!

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.290
Yep! This suits you
more than I imagined, too!

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:19.630
They do say that clothes make the woman!

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.010
Hold it, you guys!

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.510
What's all this commotion about?

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.260
M-Ms. Luvia!

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:33.850
Why are you here?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.020
Why, you ask?

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:40.020
I'm the owner
of this establishment, Carnac.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:51.080
So, this entire store belongs to Ms. Luvia.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:57.160
The original owner was Sir Davenant
who was arrested in that incident the other day.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:58.790
The Mage...

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:02.290
So that's why the architecture
is this strange.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.840
It's Magecraft designed to stimulate
customers' eagerness to purchase.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:10.300
I did change the interior decoration
quite a bit to suit my aesthetics.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.060
So that's why.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.190
Isn't this a little over the top?

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.230
I adapted some of my
Gem Magecraft here, too.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:28.740
Since you're both here, I'll give
a personal tour of the newly reborn Carnac.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.280
Come on, you're being a bit pushy.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:34.410
You guys are bored, aren't you?

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:38.790
It's not that often where all three of us
coincidentally gather in one location.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.210
I see. You're inviting us to a girls' party.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.630
All right. You're okay, too, right, Gray?

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:46.760
Sure!

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.760
So, this is a girls' party.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:50.760
I...

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.140
I'll do my best!

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:11.160
Perhaps, this is a bit too provocative?

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.410
I mean, Sir seems to still be a virgin.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.420
Is something the matter?

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:34.760
Maybe it really is a bit over the top?

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.060
Oh, you want that?

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.310
Oh no, this is...

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.600
I know.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:46.940
I'd ruin it for you if I were to buy that.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.120
Well, I have a few things to take care of,

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.160
so please relax here in the owner's room.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:04.750
Are you tired?

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.170
I was experiencing everything
for the very first time,

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.670
so I was a bit overwhelmed.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.800
London is very stimulating, isn't it?

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:12.930
Yes.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.180
Back in my homeland,

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.310
there really was nothing there.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.060
Now that Luvia has stepped out,
it's the right time.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.820
Let's chat about
what you've been wanting to hear.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.530
The Holy Grail War.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:37.320
A Magecraft battle in the Far East,
fighting over the omnipotent wish granter.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:41.410
Seven Mages and seven heroes
famous through human history

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:44.750
serving them as Servants,
fought each other.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:49.750
What kind of Servant
did Sir fight alongside?

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.260
Iskandar.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:59.010
Also known as Alexander the Great.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:02.020
It's truly a ridiculous fairy tale.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:04.770
The supposed King of Conquerors

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.730
who created one of the most prominent
empires in human history...

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.440
The King of Conquerors, Iskandar...

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:14.700
He's quite established
among the great Heroic Spirits.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.450
That's probably why
my incompetent elder brother

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.950
was able to survive
through the Holy Grail War.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:24.660
What exactly did Sir see within that battle?

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.330
That's something even I don't know.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.920
But a lad named Waver Velvet,
who survived through the ordeal,

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.920
has chosen the path of suffering
by inheriting the name "El-Melloi."

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:40.510
So, it was such an important experience
for Sir that it changed his way of life?

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.430
That's what it means.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:46.520
But then, wanting to participate
in another Holy Grail War...

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:50.440
My elder brother seems to be
quite particular about that memory.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.530
Memory...

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.150
A blackout?

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.160
Ms. Reines?

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:00.240
You guys are fine, right?

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:01.870
What was that just now?

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.460
This is...

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.960
What in the world...

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.970
Lord El-Melloi II's Case Files
｛Rail Zeppelin｝ Grace note

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.680
Nobody is here?

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:25.140
A bounded field of the magical sort.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:30.940
One so extraordinary that my Mystic Eyes
show an excessive reaction to it.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:35.990
Looks like this isn't
one of your pranks, Luviagelita.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:40.160
Of course it's not!
I'll toss that line right back at you!

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:42.660
I-In any case,

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.040
we should get out of this building.

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:49.210
Trimmau.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:57.720
Check what's beyond the door,
but do it carefully.

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.340
Yes, Master.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:10.730
Is it...

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.730
Just as I thought.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.900
This is a type of alternate space.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.480
It seems we've been severed
from the real world.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.990
I'm sure the other exits
will behave the same way.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.950
Does that mean we're trapped in here?

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:26.620
But why just the three of us...

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:31.210
Perhaps an assassination attempt
on the next head of the El-Melloi,

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:34.380
a family that also has many enemies
within the Clock Tower?

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.710
Come on now!

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:40.550
You, too, must have grudges for all
the aggressive actions you've taken, right?

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:44.220
For now, let's think of a way to escape.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.390
Can't we contact anyone outside?

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:48.020
No good.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:50.770
No electromagnetic waves
have succeeded connection for a while now.

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:54.560
That means we must get
through all of this by ourselves.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:58.280
Or do you think we should bet
on sitting here and waiting for help?

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.650
Of course the answer to that is "no."

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:05.120
I'll make whoever planned
such a ludicrous ordeal regret it!

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.660
It seems we're in agreement there.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.920
<i>Call blue, red, green...</i>

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:18.420
<i>for your queen!</i>

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:26.350
No good after all.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:29.010
This is getting rather annoying.

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:31.680
This reminds me of what happened
at the Separation Castle.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.060
Come to think of it,

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:36.310
Ms. Luvia, you got trapped
inside a bounded field back then, too.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.110
I'd like to hear the details about that.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:40.570
I reject that request!

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:44.490
And Gray, don't say things
you don't need to! Understand?

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:45.610
Yes!

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.830
But we're getting nowhere.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:53.290
It's impossible to open an escape route
with Magecraft we have on hand.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.380
Back then, Sir was with us.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:00.500
If Sir was here in a time like this...

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.760
That's it, Gray!

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.300
Indeed, if said El-Melloi II was here,

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:10.640
it would be his forte, his specialty
to dismantle such a crisis.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:11.470
What are you...

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:19.060
And fortunately, we know a little bit
of how that man teaches. His logic, his tactics.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:23.820
Well, do you mean we should try
mimicking what Sir might do?

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.400
Exactly.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.410
It seems we can't figure out
any other option.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.240
Well now, Gray...

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.200
M-Me?

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:36.000
You're the one who knows
how he does things best.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:39.670
At times like this, what would
the starting point for his logic be?

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:42.670
If it was Sir...

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:46.010
It would be "the whydunit."

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.050
That means the motive.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:53.060
Why were just the three of us
trapped in here?

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.930
That's not even worth considering.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.900
There are plenty of reasons
why someone would target us.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:58.520
Um...

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:03.280
Unlike the two of you,
I'm not that important a person.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.610
You're just a poor student

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:08.820
compared to these young ladies!

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:11.200
I don't think that's the case.

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:14.620
But if this was a plan targeting one of us,

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:17.080
it's unnatural to get
all three of us together.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:21.460
Besides, it's strange they just captured us
and haven't made any other actions.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:26.170
That's just it. Compared to how grand this
bounded field is, it's somehow a sloppy job.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:29.390
It's as if the perpetrator
isn't thinking at all.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:30.680
Um...

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:35.060
What if there is no perpetrator
from the beginning?

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.060
What do you mean by that?

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:42.730
Perhaps, it wasn't like someone
targeted us and locked us up in here.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:46.400
I see. So, not an incident
but merely an accident.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:51.200
You're suggesting that the magical structure
of this building ran out of control?

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:55.200
Are you saying there were faults
in the interior decorating that I adjusted?

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:59.000
In the name of my family, I never used
cheap spells that would do as such.

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.830
It's the reverse, "Owner."

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:03.460
It's not that there was anything lacking,

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.590
but there was just too much,
and it created an excessive reaction.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:08.920
Can't you think of it that way?

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:10.130
What the...

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.140
Th-That just can't...

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.180
So, you have an idea...

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:17.770
about what I'm talking about?

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.230
Something wrong in this hall?

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.490
I said the building was enchanted
with Magecraft

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.370
stimulating customers' eagerness
to purchase, right?

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:36.370
The key element for the spell is right here.

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:37.410
I see.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:41.290
In Magecraft, wealth springs
from underground,

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.500
and that's why we're in the basement.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.000
It's over there.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.930
Is that Gem Magecraft?

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:54.760
Yeah, way too over the top.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:16:00.180
It's just like getting carried away and
putting way too many toppings on a parfait!

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:01.770
H-Hush, you!

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:05.190
In any case, if we can
somehow deal with that...

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:16.830
This is...

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:20.120
So, the security system
is also running out of control?

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:22.250
I can see why
without you saying anything.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.170
Can't you stop it somehow?

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:27.170
My systems are perfect!

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.340
There's no way outside intervention
will be authorized!

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:32.220
All right, I get it.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.220
Trim.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.180
Yes?

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.010
Hold up.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.010
This is my store.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:40.600
I'll settle everything by myself.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:42.560
Get down.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.170
P-Pro wrestling?

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:08.880
Just look at that!

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:12.880
A graceful mannerism unleashes a department
store full of murderous techniques!

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.380
A Scandinavian human forklift!

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:20.720
Or you could call her
"Hercules revived in modern day"!

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:26.400
What the hell is that
Flat guy teaching Trim?

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:30.980
Every lady should know
about catch-as-catch-can!

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:33.740
Amazing!

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.410
So, that's what every lady
should know about!

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.120
Oh, don't go believing her, okay?

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:43.660
All we need to do now is to break this?

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:47.630
But are you fine with that?
It must cost quite a bit.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.460
It's inexpensive as the price
for the lesson I learned.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:56.630
At times, one must discard even things
that are important in order to proceed.

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:01.140
Even things that are important...

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.430
Nothing less from the head
of the Edelfelt Family.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:06.520
Well then, Trimmau?

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:08.150
Yes, Master.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.410
Oh, brother...

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.540
That was quite an adventure.

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.710
Now, to celebrate our return...

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.670
How about we have
another round of afternoon tea?

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.840
I must be careful
about all the toppings I add on.

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:47.100
We were involved
in quite the trouble today.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:50.350
Yes, but somehow it ended up being fun.

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:53.770
However, there's something
I don't understand.

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:57.570
If that was Magecraft
on a building running out of control,

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.950
what caused it to activate?

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:05.370
Oh, I can at least make a theory
in the fashion of my elder brother.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:10.170
Carnac was enchanted with Magecraft
to gather a fortune.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:14.040
In other words, it was a spell
that didn't allow fortune to escape.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:16.420
Didn't allow an escape?

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:18.300
Can it be—

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:21.430
Right. We were seen as treasures
to not be taken outside,

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:24.470
even if it meant
putting up a bounded field.

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:28.310
But I can understand
Ms. Reines or Ms. Luvia,

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.270
but I'm not that...

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.400
Come now, what are you talking about?

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.280
You have the most mystic of Mystics.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:43.030
You carry one of the most prominent
Noble Phantasms in human history!

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:48.540
Jeez. Having low self-esteem
can be questionable, too, okay?

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:50.750
O-Okay.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:53.710
Um...

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:57.760
So, this... He won't think
this is strange or anything, will he?

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:05.720
Of course not.

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:16.020
I have returned, sir.

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.190
Yeah.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:20.440
Seems like she took you around
on quite a trip.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:23.950
I'm sorry my little sister
troubles you so much.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:25.950
Oh no, not at all.

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.240
It was fun for me.

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:30.450
I see.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.210
Sir?

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:36.960
Oh, nothing.

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:42.470
Um...

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:45.850
I-If you'll excuse me...

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:48.140
Hold up!

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:52.850
Something...

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:57.400
...of utmost importance
to me has been stolen!

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:01.740
A Relic of a certain Heroic Spirit.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:02.900
That would be...

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:06.160
You heard from Reines, didn't you?

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:12.080
The Heroic Spirit that I fought alongside
in the Holy Grail War ten years ago...

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:17.170
The mantle of Iskandar.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:22.970
<i>The key for Sir to reunite with said spirit...</i>

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:30.220
All that's left inside the box
that housed the Relic was this letter.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:34.190
"We hereby invite you to our banquet.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:38.520
We request the pleasure of your company,
so we hope that you will attend by all means.

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:40.270
The Mystic Eyes Collection Train,

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:43.820
Rail Zeppelin."

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:46.570
Rail Zeppelin?

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:47.950
Yeah.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.740
It gathers any and every
Mystic Eyes out there

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:52.620
and puts them on auction once a year.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:55.120
A train full of supernatural beings.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:56.750
Then, that's where...

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:58.460
Gray...

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:00.960
Will you head out to Rail Zeppelin...

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:03.670
together with me?

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:09.970
EPISODE 6: A Girl, a Department Store, and a Gift
